WEBVTT

00:00:00.419 --> 00:00:02.310
An image gets reposted. A clip

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.329
loses its date. An answer sounds

00:00:04.354 --> 00:00:06.434
certain. But where did it come

00:00:06.712 --> 00:00:06.963
from?

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.195
Hi, I'm Vasu. I built ContextTrail.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.635
a place to follow the question

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.810
and keep the evidence.

00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:19.280
Start with an image, a video,

00:00:19.305 --> 00:00:21.655
or a question. This Earthrise run

00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:24.885
retained 13 source records with reporting

00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:26.697
origins still unresolved.

00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:31.745
Open the passage. NASA names Bill

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.275
Anders aboard Apollo 8. Keep the

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.146
publication date beside the quote. A

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.935
page date isn't the photograph's date.

00:00:42.265 --> 00:00:44.832
Pin exactly what the source supports,

00:00:44.857 --> 00:00:46.656
then select an answer sentence to

00:00:46.681 --> 00:00:48.476
inspect the evidence behind it.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.644
Questions get their own investigation. Here,

00:00:54.669 --> 00:00:57.496
12 sources, three inspected quotes, and

00:00:57.521 --> 00:00:59.125
nine leads still waiting for a

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.048
closer look.

00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:04.172
For video, each searched moment keeps

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.317
its own source trail. This lead's

00:01:06.395 --> 00:01:08.476
identity is still unconfirmed.

00:01:11.044 --> 00:01:12.953
Save the case and come back.

00:01:12.978 --> 00:01:15.064
Keep version history. Set a watch

00:01:15.089 --> 00:01:16.906
to return for new evidence.

00:01:21.005 --> 00:01:22.722
because the question doesn't end when

00:01:22.747 --> 00:01:25.679
the tab closes. ContextTrail. follow the

00:01:25.704 --> 00:01:26.500
question.
